---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Release checklist"
   summary="Public releases need one last reality check. CI covers the fast, repeatable virtual path. It does not replace real assistive technology smoke tests."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>Before a public minor or major release</h2>
      <ol>
         <li>Wait for all CI checks to pass.</li>
         <li>Run a manual macOS VoiceOver smoke pass on representative fixtures or demo targets.</li>
         <li>Run a manual Windows NVDA smoke pass on representative fixtures or demo targets.</li>
         <li>Review the deferred items for the release and make an explicit accept or block decision.</li>
         <li>Record what was exercised and any environment constraints that mattered.</li>
      </ol>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Do not skip these basic commands</h2>
      <pre><code>npm run standards
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js help-all
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js doctor --json</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Release path</h2>
      <p>
         The current release record lives in <code>releases/v0.3.0-readiness.md</code>. It spells out
         the package release path, the docs publish path, the Agent Skill release path, and the deferred
         items that still need an explicit call before a public cut.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Package, docs, and skill flow</h2>
      <ul>
         <li>Packages: publish workspace packages in dependency order after <code>npm run standards</code> passes.</li>
         <li>Docs: build <code>apps/docs/dist/</code> and publish the generated static site.</li>
         <li>Agent Skill: ship <code>skills/a11ied/</code> only after the skill text matches the released CLI and MCP behavior.</li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Deferred items</h2>
      <p>
         The current milestone still carries a few accepted rough edges. They are written down on
         purpose. Real-target smoke is still manual, and package publication is still manual.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
      <p>
         VoiceOver and NVDA are the real target platforms. The virtual reader is valuable, but it is not
         a substitute for shipping confidence on those platforms.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
